12:1  witnesses (a-11)  Witness, in English, has two senses. &amp;apos;seeing, so as to bear  witness,&amp;apos; and &amp;apos;giving testimony to.&amp;apos; The last only I apprehend  is in the Greek here.
  sin (b-19)  Or &amp;apos;the sin.&amp;apos;
  entangles (c-23)  Or &amp;apos;besets.&amp;apos; The one Greek word here represents the whole  phrase, &amp;apos;which so easily entangles us.&amp;apos;

